==Status Report: 2026-10-12 00:15 PDT==
IMPLEMENTED — one-paragraph look-ahead (builds + all tests pass). This directly
addresses your last reply: when playing straight through, the next paragraph is
now rendered *while* the current one plays, instead of only after it ends.

What changed (all in `tts/SpeechController.kt`):
  • As soon as a chunk's audio actually starts (`playFile`), the controller kicks
    off synthesis of the NEXT chunk in the background (`maybePrimeLookAhead`),
    while the current chunk keeps playing.
  • When that look-ahead render finishes it is stashed (`readyToPlayIndex`), and
    when the current chunk ends it is played immediately — no synthesis wait at
    the paragraph boundary.
  • If the look-ahead is still rendering when the current chunk ends (a genuinely
    slow engine), we wait for it rather than double-rendering, and fall back to
    on-demand synthesis only when no pre-render was in flight.
  • All the existing behavior (per-paragraph position highlight/scroll, pause →
    true MediaPlayer pause, resume, skip by section, stop) is preserved: the play
    head (`currentIndex`) still advances only when a chunk becomes audible, so the
    left margin and skip logic are unaffected. Pause/resume/skip/stop all clear
    the pre-render state safely.

Net effect: the per-paragraph delay becomes `max(synthesis, playback)` overlap
instead of `synthesis + playback` serialized. For engines where synthesis is
slower than playback (your Pocket TTS 20–30 s), a *single* paragraph of
look-ahead may not fully hide the gap if one paragraph's speech is shorter than
its render time; note the queue still re-verifies "render N+1 while N plays"
exactly as you described.

Honest scope note / possible follow-up: this is look-ahead of ONE. If Pocket TTS
is still gappy because each paragraph renders longer than it takes to speak, the
next step is a deeper look-ahead (pre-render 2–3 paragraphs ahead while playing),
which needs a small set of in-flight render indices instead of the single
`readyToPlayIndex`. I kept it to one chunk to stay low-risk to the pause/resume/
skip paths. I can extend it to multi-chunk if you say the single look-ahead isn't
enough after listening.

